      "message": "Keeping both `sec_state` and transport based security states alive leaves the door open for someone to make a mistake.\n\nHow about we initially replace `sec_state` with `le_link` and `bredr_link` without making logical changes? We will have to replace all direct access to the `sec_state` with helper functions like this:\n```\n  bool is_security_state_bredr_authenticating() const {\n    return le_link \u003d\u003d tSECURITY_STATE::AUTHENTICATING || bredr_link \u003d\u003d tSECURITY_STATE::AUTHENTICATING;\n  }\n```\n\nIn a second cl, we can then make logical changes guarded by the flag.\n```\n  bool is_security_state_bredr_authenticating() const {\n    if (!com::android::bluetooth::flags::split_sec_state()) {\n      return le_link \u003d\u003d tSECURITY_STATE::AUTHENTICATING || bredr_link \u003d\u003d tSECURITY_STATE::AUTHENTICATING;\n    }\n    return bredr_link \u003d\u003d tSECURITY_STATE::AUTHENTICATING;\n  }\n```\nI know this is too much rework but I think this would keep changes simpler to review and avoid potential mistakes.\nI would have been honestly fine with your initial approach without the flagging.",
